The root task's input frame is left a root, as every frame of its memory was
before that memory was an Untyped,
so memory that may become a pool again carries a frame that does not lie below it,
and revoking below it would leave the input mapped.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: memory that may hold kernel objects overlaps a node not above or below it
Witness: fuzz actor-handoff

diff --git a/kernel/boot.c b/kernel/boot.c
--- a/kernel/boot.c
+++ b/kernel/boot.c
@@ -131,8 +131,7 @@ struct thread *boot_create_root(void)
         }
         bool pooled = i == BOOT_CAP_CAPTABLE || i == BOOT_CAP_PROCESS || i == BOOT_CAP_THREAD ||
                       i == BOOT_CAP_POOL;
-        bool own = (i == BOOT_CAP_CODE && IN_ROOT_RAM(USER_CODE_BASE, USER_CODE_SIZE)) || i == BOOT_CAP_DATA ||
-                   (i == BOOT_CAP_INPUT && IN_ROOT_RAM(INPUT_BASE, INPUT_SIZE));
+        bool own = (i == BOOT_CAP_CODE && IN_ROOT_RAM(USER_CODE_BASE, USER_CODE_SIZE)) || i == BOOT_CAP_DATA;
         if (cap_store(table, i, &boot[i], pooled ? &pool->node : own ? root_ram : NULL) != KERR_OK) {
             kpanic("cannot fill the root task's table");
         }
